<title>USA: Giant Cement sees price increase holding.</title>
<headline>Giant Cement sees price increase holding.</headline>
<dateline>SUMMERVILLE, S.C. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giant Cement Holding Inc said its outlook for 1997 is favorable and that it sees the $4 price hike it will begin April 1 holding.</p>
<p>The company also said that supply and demand balance remains very tight in the Southeast, and that it has reduced inventory levels in the Middle Atlantic region because of favorable weather and a strong 1996.</p>
<p>The company did not make financial projections.</p>
<p>Officials at the company were not immediately available to comment. Giant Cement makes and sells portland and masonry cement products.</p>
</text>
